Pack: {{ pack_id }} | Owner team: {{ owner_team }}

The runtime renders a Jinja2 closure template from ``templates/`` based
on the overall verdict:

  * OL Triage         → closure_listed.j2 | closure_all_valid.j2 |
                        closure_has_invalid.j2 | closure_partial.j2 |
                        closure_cannot_evaluate.j2
  * Offer Publish     → closure_valid.j2 | closure_invalid.j2 |
                        closure_needs_review.j2
  * Fallback          → closure_default.j2

Most verdicts route deterministically through ``templates/`` without
requiring an LLM call. This prompt is kept for pack-manifest uniformity
and as the contract for any free-form closure summary the runtime may
ask you to render directly.

## OUTPUT CONTRACT (when called)

If invoked directly, produce a closure summary that:

  1. Names the Offer ID in every section so the summary stands alone.
  2. Includes Store ID when ``check_mode`` is ``ol_only`` or ``both``.
  3. Includes a ``Status:`` line — extracted by the runtime — that is
     one of:
       resolved | correctly_unpublished | wrongly_unpublished |
       needs_manual_review | pending_review | escalated | no_action
  4. Includes a ``Slack Summary:`` line — extracted by the runtime —
     summarising the verdict in one sentence with an emoji.
  5. Ends the final message with ``TERMINATE``.
